      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Worked example — this agent, 2026-09-20",
      "prov:value": "### Worked example — this agent, 2026-09-20\n\nAsked the repo owner to choose how a graph typology gets registered. Four options,\neach with a real cost written into its `description`, a recommendation marked,\nand a default stated. It passed every item in `interaction-modality` §4.2.\n\n**The owner dismissed it**, and asked for *\"better comparison, pros, cons,\nrecommendation, downstream impacts … given context before the question.\"*\n\nWhat was missing was not effort. The costs were there, but scattered one per\noption behind an interface that shows them singly; nothing said what each choice\n*forecloses*; and the four could not be read side by side. The preamble had\nnarrated the problem at length and then handed over four names.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20",
        "owner"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
